 \\,\\sqrt{3}/3}(12\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\pi ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504613 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "275cbf3f-d183-51d1-83d2-3cab6277b499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504613 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](images/fc/fc06a4e63f38a315dd3944f65f871cca2dbdddee26ec268e857f79e5f4ab8848.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ directly into the limit, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/3}(12\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\pi ) & =12\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})+\\pi  \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi }(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+1)^{3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ac5902a-7a9e-53bd-a352-8c43204e3720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504615 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x):$\n\n![](images/9d/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since $\\pi \\notin [-1,1],$ this means that $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\pi )$ is undefined.\n\nTherefore, our limit is undefined, too." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}))=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55ce71ca-d33d-5c8b-9d05-07e0dca2765b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504629 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch the graph of  $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}):$   \n\n![](images/4a/4abceba56f404b0b39fbde4b1f7da0ec36e69a496c4ef52d3bebfbcb8c7d3380.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$    \n\nNow, substituting $x=3$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339135" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+6}{2x+3}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "779dfcc0-3a36-5636-a5d6-b4ea61af4fcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504643 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x):$\n\n![](images/24/24f07da42a537ded7916fc2440dcf3ee1ccdfc81c7b027b47e97814fec059f5a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+6}{2x+3} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)+6}{2(0)+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1069 "q-302680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78505148-e7b2-516b-80ad-17e7629d4193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504644 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/24/24f07da42a537ded7916fc2440dcf3ee1ccdfc81c7b027b47e97814fec059f5a.png)\n\n \n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+5}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81d25b33-02da-5a6a-a064-091425605527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504648 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](images/ca/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+5} & =\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)}{(0)^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(0)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{5} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cdfb619c-431d-5983-938b-5503bb7b30f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504684 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/85/85a182aabfe64c27eaafde94e3bdbede9409b02cfd87395cb2fc5543b09c4e05.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }6\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x))=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0a1a56f-e520-52c2-bfca-2937cd7b17ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504686 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x):$ \n\n![](images/87/873a6fb793d2ae68eab172132e467a48a43ab84733ad92155fe6cc012f516382.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }6\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x))=6\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})=3\\pi .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
